# Pipeline-generated SQLite (regenerate with pipeline/phase3.mjs; the CSV
# sheets + *.json facts are the source of truth for historical stats)
data/*.db

# Phase 2's per-year scratch file. It writes one beside the merged facts on
# every run — the same rows the backbone and matchfacts files already hold, cut
# to one year. Nothing reads them; they are a byproduct of a rebuild, and ten
# of them appearing untracked after `npm run build:editions` is noise.
data/bourbon-cup-*-full.json

# Local Firebase project override (see .env.example). `*.local` above already
# covers .env.local; this catches a bare .env too.
.env

# Claude Code: settings.json and launch.json are shared so both developers'
# agents behave the same way. Personal permission grants stay out.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Firebase service-account keys. `scripts/import-history.mjs` needs one, and
# the console downloads it under this name — into whatever folder the browser
# saves to, which is sometimes this one. The key bypasses firestore.rules
# entirely, so a commit of it hands the whole database to anyone who reads the
# repo. Ignored by the pattern the console itself names the file with, in every
# directory, so it cannot be added by accident.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
serviceAccount*.json

# ── The iOS build (see docs/app-store.md) ──
# `ios/` IS tracked, unlike the Android project, and the difference is that
# this one is edited by hand. Info.plist carries the usage strings and the
# export-compliance flag, App.entitlements carries push and Sign in with
# Apple, PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy is the privacy manifest, and the pbxproj holds
# iPhone-only and the entitlements path. Regenerating it would lose all of
# that; `ios/.gitignore` already covers the parts that ARE generated (the
# copied web build, the derived data, the config files Capacitor writes).
#
# GoogleService-Info.plist is not tracked. It is downloaded from the Firebase
# console and dragged into Xcode, which is also what creates its project
# reference — so committing the file without the reference would look present
# and do nothing. Without it the app builds and push silently never works.
ios/App/App/GoogleService-Info.plist

# ── The Android build (see docs/play-store.md) ──
# `twa-manifest.json` IS tracked — it is the configuration, and it is what
# makes `bubblewrap build` reproducible on another machine. Everything
# Bubblewrap generates FROM it is not: the Gradle project is a build artifact
# and regenerating it is one command.
android.keystore
*.keystore
*.jks
app-release-bundle.aab
app-release-signed.apk
/app/
/gradle/
gradlew
gradlew.bat
build.gradle
settings.gradle
gradle.properties
store_icon.png

